<h2>How to use this page</h2>
<p>Each template has a label like "<em>Reply A: schedule discovery call (phase 01)</em>" so you can scan to the one you need. Curly-brace placeholders <code>&#123;like_this&#125;</code> get replaced with real values. Don't change the structure unless you have a reason; the wording is tuned to convert without being pushy.</p>

<h2>Phase 01 &middot; First contact</h2>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">A &middot; Schedule discovery call (strong fit)</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Thanks for reaching out, {specific_reference_to_their_email}.

Sounds like a good fit for what we do. Want to grab 20 minutes to talk
through what you're looking for and what we'd build? No pitch deck, no
pressure. The first call is just us asking what you've got and what you
want.

Pick a slot here: {calendar_link}

Or reply with a few times that work and I'll confirm.

— Jon
Pikes Peak Web Designs
{phone}</pre>
</div>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">B &middot; Not yet ready</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Appreciate you reaching out. Sounds like a good potential fit; just not
the right moment to start a build.

I'll bookmark this and circle back in {timeframe}. If you want to move
faster, our /what-we-build/ page has the full deliverable laid out:
https://pikespeakwebdesigns.com/what-we-build/

In the meantime, no pressure. Reach out any time you want to talk.

— Jon</pre>
</div>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">C &middot; Out of scope, refer out</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Thanks for the note. Honest answer: this isn't our specialty. We focus
on small US/Canadian service businesses on flat-rate marketing sites;
what you're describing is {their_actual_need}, which is a different
shape of build.

{recommended_specialist} does this well; their site is {url}. I have
no financial relationship with them, just sending you toward someone
who can do right by you.

Best of luck with the project.

— Jon</pre>
</div>

<h2>Phase 03 &middot; Proposal &amp; agreement</h2>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Proposal cover note</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Good talking earlier. Quick proposal below based on what we discussed.
Nothing fancy; just what I'd build, the timeline, and what it costs.

{paste_proposal_or_link}

If it looks right, sign here: https://pikespeakwebdesigns.com/agreement/
If you want to tweak something, reply with what you'd change. No
pressure either way; this offer holds for 30 days.

— Jon
{phone}</pre>
</div>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">7-day proposal follow-up</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Following up on the proposal I sent {date}. Anything need clarifying?

If timing isn't right, no problem; let me know and I'll bookmark this
for later. If yes, the agreement link is the same:
https://pikespeakwebdesigns.com/agreement/

— Jon</pre>
</div>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Agreement-signed receipt</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Signed agreement received. Welcome aboard.

Kickoff call is on the calendar for {date_time}. In the meantime, the
onboarding form will give us everything I need to start: nine sections,
~20 minutes to fill out, save and reload as you go.

https://pikespeakwebdesigns.com/onboarding/

I will start the design the day after the kickoff call. Launch target:
{date}.

— Jon</pre>
</div>

<h2>Phase 04 &middot; Onboarding</h2>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Kickoff confirmation</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Good kickoff. Quick recap so I am aligned:

LAUNCH WINDOW: {date_range}
ASSETS NEEDED BY: {date}
COMMUNICATION: {email primary, text for urgent}
DECISION-MAKER ON DESIGN: {name}

Asset upload link: {drive_folder_link}
Onboarding form (if not done): https://pikespeakwebdesigns.com/onboarding/

I'll start the wireframe today. First design preview in your inbox by
{preview_date}. Until then I won't bug you; if questions come up on
my end, I'll batch them into one email rather than ping you piecemeal.

Anything you remember after this email, just send it. I can absorb
late additions; we just can't start without the basics above.

— Jon
{phone}</pre>
</div>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Asset reminder (3 days post-kickoff)</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Heads up: I'm waiting on {missing_assets} before I can start the
{design / specific page}.

If you can get those over by {target_date}, I will keep the launch on
schedule. If you need more time, let me know what's realistic and I'll
adjust the launch window.

Drive link to drop them in: {drive_folder_link}

— Jon</pre>
</div>

<h2>Phase 05 &middot; Design</h2>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Round 1 send</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

First-round design is ready. Link below.

{notion_or_doc_link}

What to look for:
- Does the homepage layout fit how you'd want a customer to read it?
- Do the type and color choices feel like you?
- Is the copy in the right voice? (I will keep tweaking; this is the
  starting draft.)

Highlight + comment anywhere in the doc. Don't hold back; honest notes
get to the right design faster than polite ones.

Aim to get notes back within 5 business days. Round 2 lands ~5 days
after that.

— Jon</pre>
</div>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Round 2 send (clickable preview)</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Round 2 is up. This is a real working preview — you can click around,
fill out the contact form (test mode, no real submission), see it on
your phone.

{preview_url}

What I built since round 1:
- {bullet_changes}

Use the design feedback form when you're ready. Or reply with notes
by section if that's easier.

https://pikespeakwebdesigns.com/design-feedback/

We typically wrap design in one more round after this. If I need a
third, no problem; the agreement covers unlimited revisions.

— Jon</pre>
</div>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Pre-build sign-off confirmation</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Great. Confirming: design is approved as of today. I'll start the
build this week.

What's next:
- Build phase, ~10 business days.
- Pre-launch QA right after.
- Launch window: still {launch_date_range}.

Any last design changes after this point are still doable; they just
slot into the build phase rather than the design phase. Big restructures
would push the timeline.

— Jon</pre>
</div>

<h2>Phase 06 &middot; Build</h2>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Mid-build status update (weekly)</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Quick status:

PROGRESS: {what's done since last update}
NEXT: {what's coming this week}
ANY QUESTIONS FOR YOU: {none / 1-2 items}

Preview URL is updated as I push: {url}
On track for {launch_date}.

— Jon</pre>
</div>

<h2>Phase 07 &middot; Pre-launch QA</h2>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Pre-launch sign-off email</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Build is QA-clean. Launch-ready.

PREVIEW URL: {preview_url}
LAUNCH WINDOW: {date_range}
LIGHTHOUSE SCORES: {mobile_perf} / {mobile_a11y} / {mobile_bp} / {mobile_seo} mobile
LIGHTHOUSE DESKTOP: {desktop_perf} / {desktop_a11y} / {desktop_bp} / {desktop_seo}

Walk through the preview URL one more time. Check anything you'd want
changed. After today, changes can still happen but they're "post-
launch" content updates rather than build-phase changes.

If you sign off, reply with "go" and I'll launch on {launch_date}.
The launch itself takes about 30 minutes; you don't need to be
available unless we hit a snag.

— Jon</pre>
</div>

<h2>Phase 08 &middot; Launch</h2>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Launch confirmation</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Live.

NEW URL: https://{domain}/
LAUNCH TIME: {timestamp}
LIGHTHOUSE: {scores}

What I just did:
- Migrated DNS to point at our hosting
- Provisioned SSL (HTTPS works without warning)
- Submitted the sitemap to Google Search Console
- Set up uptime monitoring (1-minute checks)
- Wired the contact form to your inbox

What you should do today:
- Click through your site, especially on your phone
- Submit your contact form once to verify it lands in {their_inbox}
- Check your Google Business Profile and update any phone/address
  references if they pointed to the old site path

What happens next:
- The owner's guide (https://pikespeakwebdesigns.com/owners-guide/)
  walks through everything I'll handle and what you might want to do
  occasionally
- Content updates: just email me. Same-day for routine changes.
- Emergencies: call/text me directly: {phone}
- The next 2-3 days I'll be watching analytics + uptime closely. If
  anything looks off, I'll catch it.

You're done.

— Jon</pre>
</div>

<h2>Phase 09 &middot; Maintenance</h2>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Acknowledge update request</div>
<pre>Got it, {first_name}. Working on this today; you'll have confirmation
by EOD.

— J</pre>
</div>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Confirm complete</div>
<pre>Done. Changes are live at {url}.

If you see anything not quite right, reply and I'll adjust.

— J</pre>
</div>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Quote needed for non-routine work</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Want to scope this before I start, since it's a bit beyond the usual
content update.

WHAT YOU DESCRIBED: {their_request}
WHAT IT'D INVOLVE: {bullets, plain language}
ESTIMATE: {hours / fixed cost}
TIMELINE: {when it'd be ready}

If that works, reply "go" and I'll start tomorrow. If you want to scope
something narrower, let me know and I'll re-quote.

— J</pre>
</div>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Quarterly check-in</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Q-check-in. Site's been live {months} now.

LAST 90 DAYS:
- Page views: {n}
- Top pages: {bullets}
- Form submissions: {n}
- Uptime: {pct}
- Lighthouse: {scores stable / improving / regressed}

ANYTHING I NOTICED:
{1-3 observations}

ANYTHING I'D RECOMMEND:
{1-2 things, no pressure}

If you want to talk through any of it, 20 min next week works.

— J</pre>
</div>

<h2>Phase 10 &middot; Emergencies</h2>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Initial acknowledgment (within 5 min)</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Got the alert. Looking at it now. I'll have an update for you within
15 minutes.

— Jon
{phone}</pre>
</div>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Status update during incident</div>
<pre>Update at {time}: {what's happening}. {What I'm trying or waiting on}.
Next update at {time + 15-30 min}.</pre>
</div>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">All clear</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Resolved as of {time}.

WHAT HAPPENED: {one paragraph, plain language}
HOW IT'S FIXED: {one paragraph}
DURATION: site was {affected level} from {start} to {end} ({duration}).

Full writeup tomorrow. If anything else looks off in the meantime,
call/text and I'll jump on it.

— Jon</pre>
</div>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Post-incident writeup (24 hours later)</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Quick post-mortem for yesterday's incident. Honest version, not
corporate.

WHAT HAPPENED:
{plain narrative}

ROOT CAUSE:
{specific, technical or operational}

WHAT WE FIXED IMMEDIATELY:
{bullets}

WHAT WE'LL DO DIFFERENTLY:
{one or two concrete process changes}

If you want to walk through any of this on a call, my time's free.

— Jon</pre>
</div>

